  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e2c84346-9115-40a2-81cd-ce68a86a9103",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -96,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 1012,
        "height": 1012,
        "content": "## 🏫 AI-Powered Teacher Substitute Automation (— Multi-Candidate + Confirmation Loop)\n\n### How it works\nWhen a teacher submits a leave request, the workflow finds affected classes, asks AI to rank the TOP 3 substitute candidates per class, filters out anyone already double-booked, then sends the top candidate a live confirmation request. If they decline or don't respond in time, the workflow automatically retries with the next-ranked candidate — up to 3 attempts — before escalating to a human admin for manual selection.\n\nOnce a substitute confirms, the workflow blocks their calendar, emails + SMS's them the details, updates records, and notifies students. A separate weekly scheduled branch aggregates substitute workload and posts a fairness digest to Slack.\n\n### What's new vs. v1\n1. **Conflict check** — cross-references each candidate against today's already-assigned substitutes before offering the slot\n2. **Ranked candidates (top 3)** from the AI, not a single pick\n3. **Human-in-the-loop confirmation** — substitute must accept/decline via Telegram Send-and-Wait before anything is finalized\n4. **Automatic retry/escalation loop** — declined or timed-out candidates are skipped and the next one tried; after 3 failed attempts it escalates to the admin\n5. **Google Calendar block** for the confirmed substitute\n6. **SMS backup notification** via Twilio alongside email\n7. **Audit log** sheet separate from the payroll sheet\n8. **Weekly Substitute Workload Digest** — independent schedule-triggered branch that reports fairness/utilization to Slack\n\n### Setup steps\n1. **Google Sheets** — connect OAuth2, update spreadsheet IDs (Timetable, Substitutes, Payroll, AuditLog)\n2. **Gmail** — connect OAuth2 for substitute/student emails\n3. **OpenAI** — add API key to the AI ranking node\n4. **Telegram** — connect bot credential, set admin chat ID and replace substitute chat ID mapping\n5. **Twilio** — connect account SID/auth token for SMS backup\n6. **Google Calendar** — connect OAuth2, set target calendar ID\n7. **Slack** — connect OAuth2 for the weekly digest and error alerts\n8. Test with pinned form data, then activate"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
